Subject: Justification for Cantor M2B Platform Location Classification Revision

& [Claim] is corrective
  + [statement] replace the physically false conjunctive completion with disjoint local-volume and remote-protocol completions
  + [confidence] is high for local correction and unproven physically for remote classification

& [Support] is exact
  + [physical] the local NTFS root returned remote-query error 87
  + [honesty] no protocol-zero structure was observed
  + [local_evidence] volume-GUID and volume-information success are the products actually needed for local eligibility
  + [remote_evidence] successful nonzero remote-protocol structure is the product needed for remote rejection

& [WhySum] is structural
  + [false_option] make remote protocol optional inside one complete record
  + [rejection] absence would conflate not queried, unsupported, failed, and not applicable
  + [solution] two complete variants make required and forbidden fields compiler visible

& [WhyRequestVersion] is compatibility preserving
  + [reason] request profile 0.1 requires result 0.2
  + [result] request profile 0.2 explicitly binds result 0.3

& [Counterarguments] are answered
  + [counterargument] treat error 87 as local success
  + [answer] Microsoft defines invalid parameter, not universal locality
  + [counterargument] remove remote classification entirely
  + [answer] fail-closed remote rejection remains a requirement but can be a conditional branch

& [Invalidation] is explicit
  + [condition] source drift, synthesized evidence, profile ambiguity, product overlap, branch drift, new effect, failed local fixture, remote physical overclaim, or stale evidence
  + [response] stop and reprocess

& [Rollback] is direct
  + [forms] restore profile 0.2
  + [runtime] restore runtime 0.1 blocked behavior
  + [physical_evidence] remains immutable history
